<h2>The rebrand and relaunch</h2>
<p>In November 2026 the archive returned as ArtCard.LA. The new name is the one people already used for the cards, and it marks a new home for the same collection — {{ groups.stats.artworks }} ArtCards published on LA-Artist.com between {{ groups.stats.first | niceDate }} and {{ groups.stats.last | niceDate }}.</p>
<p>You will still see LA-Artist.com on the original cards, in the books, and in earlier exhibitions. ArtCard.LA is where the archive lives now. You can also follow the archive on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/artcard.la/">Instagram</a>.</p>
<h2>About this archive</h2>
<p>ArtCard.LA is a static archive of those published ArtCards. Each card is listed under the artist name and ZIP code written on it, as recorded on the original site. Cards without a usable ZIP code are grouped under <a href="{{ '/region/outside-la/' | url }}">Outside LA / California</a>, <a href="{{ '/region/us-states/' | url }}">U.S. States</a>, <a href="{{ '/region/international/' | url }}">International</a> and <a href="{{ '/region/unknown/' | url }}">Unknown</a>. Images are shown at the size they were originally published.</p>
<p>All artworks remain © their artists.</p>
